From 5559957a8f23a83f74241f64ef523bbea1d5c828 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GrgaPalcic <26028466+GrgaPalcic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 10:30:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: the SSD tier under shared pages beside
 TF_GLM_KV_SHARD

The sharded writer and the recall into one part, per-rank disk ops (key_put, lat_put, lat_take, slot_put, slot_take, page_put, page_take), the store's own identity. Measured on two DGX Sparks before the rebase onto 0001-0121 (2026-11-10, 16-row windows): a 606,208-token state resumes after a restart in 7.05 s to first token with the cold reply's sha256 (4080 MiB read in 3.1 s), and after eviction by two other 600k conversations in 7.15 s.
